---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/site/PageHead.astro';
import PipelineFlow from '../components/site/PipelineFlow.astro';
---

<Site
    title="Climate data pipelines for parametric insurance · Skaraz Data"
    description="Trigger and index pipelines for parametric insurance: built inside your stack and handed over with tests, docs and runbook, or run by Skaraz Data as calculation agent. Onboarding one index from EUR 10,000."
>
    <PageHead
        label="Service · pipelines · onboarding from EUR 10,000"
        title="Your trigger pipeline, built inside your team or run by your calculation agent."
        lede="The machinery behind every calculation on this site, built for your perils and your countries. You choose where it runs and who owns it."
    />

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="grid cols-2">
                <div class="card opt reveal" style="--i:0">
                    <p class="label">Option A · handed over</p>
                    <h3>I build it in your stack, your team owns it.</h3>
                    <p class="muted">Code in your repository, tests, documentation and a runbook. Pipeline support and independent verification can follow, from EUR 8,000 a year: I maintain it and check its results against the contract.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="card opt reveal" style="--i:1">
                    <p class="label">Option B · calculation agent</p>
                    <h3>I run it on my server and issue the event report.</h3>
                    <p class="muted">Scheduled pulls, checks, index and the event report the payout follows. From EUR 12,000 a year, available about six weeks after signature and set up per contract.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tint">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">What gets built</p>
                <h2>Single-job modules with checks between every step.</h2>
                <p class="lede">Each module does one job and checks its inputs before it runs. Known dataset defects are caught where they enter, not after a payout.</p>
            </div>
            <PipelineFlow />
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">Where this comes from</p>
                <h2>Two years of production pipelines at a parametric insurtech.</h2>
                <p class="lede">At Raincoat I owned the satellite and reanalysis acquisition layer (CHIRPS, ERA5-Land, IMERG, Copernicus CDS, WEkEO), shipped the Water Balance peril to production on Kubernetes, and built the Heat Stress pipeline.</p>
                <p class="muted small">CHIRPS v2 production ends after December 2026; new rainfall pipelines use CHIRPS v3.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid cols-3">
                <div class="metric reveal" style="--i:0"><span class="value num">10,000</span><span class="note">EUR, from: onboarding one index (definition, pipeline, backtest, methodology report)</span></div>
                <div class="metric reveal" style="--i:1"><span class="value num">2 to 3</span><span class="note">days of paid scoping to frame a larger or multi-peril build before quoting it</span></div>
                <div class="metric reveal" style="--i:2"><span class="value">FR · EN</span><span class="note">documentation in either language</span></div>
            </div>
            <p class="more"><a class="link" href="/projects/case-study-raincoat">Read the Raincoat case study <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Site>

<style>
    .opt { display: grid; gap: 12px; align-content: start; }
    .more { margin-top: 32px; }
</style>
